// Function to compare two canonical binary strings (arrays of chars).
// Returns:
// -1 if s1 < s2
//  0 if s1 == s2
//  1 if s1 > s2
//
// Precondition (requires):
// - s1 and s2 are non-empty
// - each element is '0' or '1'
// - canonical form: either length=1 and contains '0', or first char is '1'
